Marelle is designed with Hermes Agent and OpenCode as references. The look of
its interactive terminal interface follows the look of the Hermes Agent CLI
(banner, status line, framed answers); the art, the colours and the code are
Marelle's own. At the time of writing, no source code from either project is
included in this repository.

If code from Hermes Agent, OpenCode or any other project is added, record it
in this file with its copyright line and license, and keep the original
license text alongside the code. For MIT-licensed code, the full MIT license
text must travel with copies of the code. Only add code under licenses that
are compatible with AGPL-3.0-only, such as MIT, BSD, Apache-2.0 and
AGPL-3.0 itself.


Rust crates
===========

Marelle is built from open-source Rust crates, all under permissive licenses
(MIT, Apache-2.0, ISC, BSD-3-Clause, Unicode-3.0, Unlicense and
CDLA-Permissive-2.0). Their names, versions and license texts are listed in
THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt, which is included in every release archive. To
regenerate it, run scripts/third-party-licenses.py.
